  "_about": "a crested porcupine SCULPTED on its rig (2026-11-06, gen: scratchpad sc/new6/porcupine.py): 70 cm of stocky rodent low on short legs, a blunt dark rounded face with small eyes and small round ears; coarse black-brown hair below, and over the back and rump a coat of long quills (bodymesh.js coat, `bands`: black and white, sharp-banded, white-tipped) lying back and raised into a fan over the rump, the longest there, and a crest of long bristles (the same coat, `coat` over 1: longer) along the head and the neck; a short tail; it shuffles SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- claw, hclaw (8 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): small round cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`) close to the head; the roots faired. WHISKERS (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sharp/whiskers.py): 9 @whisker-coloured whiskers a side, 3 rows on the whisker pad (80-120 mm) -- `whiskers` shapes (bodyspec.js whiskerStrands: thin pointed strands, mirrored, on the head, near mesh only; details, so every coat and variant still shares one mesh), replacing the hand-placed cones.",
